        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Abbottsburg, North Carolina\n- People: Joseph Carter Abbott\n- Companies: Cape Fear Building Company\n- Roles: president, Union Army colonel, brevet brigadier general of volunteers, United States Senator\n- Events: American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph Carter Abbott was born on July 15, 1825.\n- Joseph Carter Abbott was a Union Army colonel during the American Civil War.\n- Joseph Carter Abbott was awarded the grade of brevet brigadier general of volunteers.\n- Joseph Carter Abbott served as a Republican United States Senator from North Carolina from 1868 to 1871.\n- Abbottsburg, North Carolina, was named for Joseph Carter Abbott.\n- Joseph Carter Abbott was president of the Cape Fear Building Company.\n- Joseph Carter Abbott died on October 8, 1881.",
